  "summary_en": "Washington State statute governing testing of autonomous (SAE level 4-5) vehicles on public roads under a department self-certification pilot program. It requires registration information, insurance proof, collision and violation reporting, advance notice to law enforcement, and public reporting to the legislature.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Testing requires self-certification with contact, jurisdictions, VINs and proof of insurance before operation.",
   "Collisions and moving violations during testing must be reported, including whether the automated system was driving; annual report due February 1.",
   "Advance written notice of 14-60 days to local law enforcement or state patrol is required.",
   "Department may charge fees, must publish information and report annually to transportation committees.",
   "'Autonomous' means SAE J3016 level 4 or 5 driving automation."
  ],
